      { id: "soc-st-2-s6t2-intro", type: "info", content: "**Tourism in Ghana**\\\\n\\\\nGhana is blessed with abundant tourist attractions — from beautiful beaches and national parks to historic castles and vibrant cultural festivals. Tourism is one of the fastest-growing sectors of Ghana's economy.\\\\n\\\\nIn this lesson, we will explore Ghana's major tourist attractions and the potential of the tourism industry." },
      { id: "soc-st-2-s6t2-content-1", type: "info", content: "**Major Tourist Attractions in Ghana**\\\\n\\\\n**Historical and Heritage Sites:**\\\\n• **Cape Coast Castle and Elmina Castle:** UNESCO World Heritage sites, reminders of the trans-Atlantic slave trade\\\\n• **Kwame Nkrumah Memorial Park:** Dedicated to Ghana's first President\\\\n• **Fort Christiansborg (Osu Castle):** Seat of government for many years\\\\n• **Independence Square:** Symbol of Ghana's freedom\\\\n\\\\n**Natural Attractions:**\\\\n• **Kakum National Park:** Canopy walkway, rainforest, diverse wildlife\\\\n• **Mole National Park:** Largest wildlife reserve in Ghana, elephants and antelopes\\\\n• **Wli Waterfalls:** Highest waterfall in West Africa\\\\n• **Lake Volta:** The largest man-made lake in the world\\\\n• **Boti Falls:** Twin waterfalls in the Eastern Region\\\\n• **Ada and Kokrobite Beaches:** Beautiful coastal resorts\\\\n\\\\n**Cultural Attractions:**\\\\n• **Panafest:** Pan-African Historical Theatre Festival\\\\n• **Homowo Festival (Ga):** Harvest festival\\\\n• **Aboakyer Festival (Effutu):** Deer hunting festival\\\\n• **Bakatue Festival (Elmina):** Fishing festival\\\\n• **Kente weaving villages:** Bonwire in Ashanti Region" },
      { id: "soc-st-2-s6t2-content-2", type: "info", content: "**Developing Tourism in Ghana**\\\\n\\\\n**Strengths of Ghana's Tourism Industry:**\\\\n• Rich cultural heritage and history\\\\n• Political stability\\\\n• Warm and welcoming people\\\\n• Diverse attractions (beaches, parks, castles, festivals)\\\\n• English-speaking country\\\\n\\\\n**Challenges Facing the Tourism Industry:**\\\\n• Inadequate infrastructure (roads, airports, hotels)\\\\n• Limited marketing and promotion\\\\n• High cost of domestic air travel\\\\n• Seasonal nature of tourism\\\\n• Competition from other destinations\\\\n• Conservation and maintenance of sites\\\\n\\\\n**Strategies to Boost Tourism:**\\\\n• Improve infrastructure\\\\n• Train more tour guides and hospitality staff\\\\n• Promote domestic tourism among Ghanaians\\\\n• Use digital marketing to reach international tourists\\\\n• Develop new attractions and experiences\\\\n• Protect and maintain existing sites\\\\n• Encourage community participation in tourism" },
      { id: "soc-st-2-s6t2-activity-1", type: "info", content: "**Activity 6.2 — Promoting Ghanaian Tourism**\\\\n\\\\nDesign a poster or short video promoting one tourist attraction in Ghana. Include:\\\\n1. The name and location of the attraction\\\\n2. What makes it special\\\\n3. How visitors can get there\\\\n4. Why people should visit\\\\n\\\\nDisplay your poster in class or share your video with classmates." },
      { id: "soc-st-2-s6t2-exercise", type: "question", content: "Test your understanding:", exercise: { question: "Which national park in Ghana is famous for its canopy walkway?", options: ["Mole National Park", "Kakum National Park", "Shai Hills Reserve", "Digya National Park"], correctIndex: 1, explanation: "Kakum National Park is famous for its canopy walkway, a series of suspension bridges high above the rainforest floor." } },
      { id: "soc-st-2-s6t2-summary", type: "info", content: "✅ **Key Takeaways: Tourism in Ghana**\\\\n\\\\nIn this lesson, you learned about:\\\\n• Major tourist attractions in Ghana (historical, natural, cultural)\\\\n• The strengths and challenges of Ghana's tourism industry\\\\n• Strategies to develop and promote tourism\\\\n\\\\nTourism has great potential to contribute to Ghana's economic development." },
      { id: "soc-st-2-s6t2-checkpoint", type: "checkpoint", content: "Check your understanding", checkpoint: { title: "Tourism in Ghana — Quick Check", passThreshold: 60, bonusXp: 20, questions: [ { question: "Which festival is celebrated by the people of Elmina?", options: ["Homowo", "Bakatue", "Aboakyer", "Damba"], correctIndex: 1, explanation: "Bakatue is a fishing festival celebrated by the people of Elmina." }, { question: "What is a major challenge facing Ghana's tourism industry?", options: ["Too many tourists", "Inadequate infrastructure", "No attractions", "Ghanaians dislike tourism"], correctIndex: 1, explanation: "Inadequate infrastructure including roads, airports, and hotels is a major challenge facing Ghana's tourism industry." } ] } }
